{
  "$comment": "Camera Motion templates. All rates are per second; total amplitude = rate x duration. zoom_rate: fraction/s (0.03 = 3%/s scale change, positive = push in). pan_rate: fraction of image width/s. rot_rate: degrees/s. parallax_target: median residual parallax as fraction of image width/s the renderer should produce for a mid-depth-range scene. Recalibrated v3: the original v2 rates were tuned defensively around a fallback geometric depth provider (no real object segmentation, ~0.3 confidence) which forced the Motion Budget Engine to throttle strength and parallax on almost every shot, and produced motion too faint to read as a real camera move. With the neural depth provider (Depth Anything V2, correct per-object structure, ~0.9 confidence) as the default, rates were raised ~1.7-2x and re-validated against the quality gates on real photographs.",
